Read `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root before changing anything; it is the single source of project rules for both Cursor and Claude Code.

Key points:
- Content JSON in `content/lessons/` is the source of truth; `media/` is generated by `tools/build_audio.py` and `dist/` by `tools/build_web.py`. Never hand-edit generated files.
- Audio is generated once at build time, never per play. CI never runs a TTS engine.
- No backend and no secrets in `web/`. Recordings never leave the device.
- Feminine-learner variants (`f`) are required wherever the learner says, or is addressed with, a gendered form.
- Simplified Roman scheme (see `docs/CONTENT_GUIDE.md`).
- Run `python3 tools/validate_content.py`, `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/unit` and `npx playwright test` before finishing a task.
